<BaseLayout title="Introduction">
  <h1>Introduction</h1>
  <p>This reference is organized around the major systems and ownership tasks associated with the 2021-model-year, third-generation Volvo S60 range. It is designed as a structured owner encyclopedia: start with the vehicle configuration, then browse the relevant system, maintenance topic or repair overview.</p>
  <h2>In this section</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="../introduction/about/">About this reference</a> — scope, source standards and safety boundaries.</li>
    <li><a href="../introduction/specifications/">Vehicle specifications</a> — powertrains, trims, drivetrain and identification notes.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Model identification</h2>
  <p>This reference covers the 2021 S60 range. North American examples include T5 gasoline, T6 gasoline and T8 Recharge plug-in hybrid powertrains, with different drivetrain and trim combinations. Availability and equipment differ by market and build date. Use the VIN-linked build information and installed labels to identify an individual car before applying specifications or ordering parts.</p>
  <h2>Three drivetrain layouts to keep separate</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>T5 FWD:</strong> front-wheel drive, without the mechanical rear-drive hardware used on AWD variants.</li>
    <li><strong>T5 AWD / T6 AWD:</strong> mechanical all-wheel drive; engine and transmission drive the front axle with a mechanical path to the rear.</li>
    <li><strong>T8 Recharge:</strong> plug-in hybrid with an electrically driven rear axle and high-voltage components; do not use mechanical-AWD diagrams as a parts map for T8.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Begin with <a href="../technical/engine-and-drivetrain/">Engine and drivetrain</a> for the powertrain comparison, or the <a href="../parts/">visual parts atlas</a> for component-area navigation.</p>
</BaseLayout>
